Z||000000||Greg Piet||08-29-2000||07:54 AM||||I just started autocrossing in the SCCA (region 72)this year with my 85 SE (6 cyl) in C-Stock<BR>Well the season is winding down (only 8 more events).<P>As of present I have won 3 of the past 4 events in my class, and I have a secure lead in the season points for the entire season.  It appears the only way for me to lose is to miss 1/2 the events which is not going to happen, and one guy to come in first place at 6 out of the 8 events with a top 3 finsih in the other two(which is highly unlikely).<P>I am getting comments from drivers with their big beefy V8's telling me I am pretty fast, and the overheard conversations normally contain "damn that kid is pretty fast in that Fiero"<P>Moral of the Story:  The stock Fiero can still kick a little ass!||||reg||1
